WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.102
Fox Corporation Chairman Rupert Murdoch.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.303
Democratic leader

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:03.903
Senator Chuck

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.138
Schumer and Congressman

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.274
Hakeem Jeffries are demanding that Fox

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.242
stop, quote,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.710
spreading false election

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.878
narratives, unquote.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.147
Jeffries spoke about this earlier today.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.550
Perhaps it's time

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.651
for America

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.087
to be able to move past that big lie.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.856
And an important step

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.723
would be those

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.458
who know it was a big lie

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.927
to publicly repudiated.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:28.695
This demand comes

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.697
in the wake of those damaging,

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.566
damning depositions and communications

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.068
and Dominion's lawsuit

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.036
against Fox

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.738
revealing the top posts and executives

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.274
knowingly aired and even spoke.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.443
Election lies on the network

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.211
knowing they were lies.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:45.912
Let's discuss

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:46.946
with former Democratic South

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:47.480
Carolina state

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.082
representative Bakari Sellers

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:49.949
along with the editor

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.751
in chief of The Dispatch, Jonah Goldberg.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.787
We should note that Jonah was subpoenaed

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.288
and deposed by Dominion

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.357
in this lawsuit against Fox,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.124
and we're not going to

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.325
ask him about that.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.427
He can't talk about it.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.162
But Jonah, let me start with you.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.764
You can't talk about your deposition,

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.966
but you can talk about Rupert Murdoch's.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.102
You were with Fox for many years.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.371
Were you surprised by all the

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.407
candor and admissions that, yes,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.842
we were spreading lies

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.010
and we knew it was lies,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.477
but we did it

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:20.313
because of money and ratings

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.014
Yeah.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.681
I mean, there's

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.148
this weird

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.317
dichotomy between shock and surprise.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.252
I'm not really surprised,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.987
but Rupert Murdoch.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.191
Rupert Murdoch is a canny, smart player.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.692
And when he just

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.827
baldly says

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.161
this wasn't about red or blue,

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.329
this was about green,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.164
talking about why he put Mike

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.100
Lindell the pillow guy back on air,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.835
because he's a big advertiser.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.703
You can almost hear his,

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.003
you know,

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:44.938
Rupert's lawyers

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.040
taking out the black tar heroin and

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.409
and tightening in the

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.111
the center on their arms.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.645
I mean, like like it's amazing

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.313
that he would say

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.280
some of these things

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.149
and not try to obfuscate

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.417
or dodge the Question

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.551
Time and time again,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.720
both in the text messages

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.956
and in the depositions,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.291
you have senior Fox executives

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.161
just saying the quiet part out loud over

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.162
and over again.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:09.896
And it's really

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.131
it's it's really compelling,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.999
even if there's, you know,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.100
more that we need to know

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.568
from the Dominion response because,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.035
you know, again,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:16.703
this is essentially

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.271
a prosecutor is brief,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.038
but it's very hard

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:19.472
not to see

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.208
this is as overwhelmingly persuasive

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.510
on the thrust of it.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.378
So, Bakari, play a little game with me.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.414
You'll like it if MSNBC is chair

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.116
admitted under oath

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.451
that their hosts

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.520
lied to their progressive viewers

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.889
just for ratings about a topic

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:36.623
that had caused

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.590
a deadly riot

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.224
at the Capitol

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.426
against a Republican president.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:40.994
What do you think

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.929
the response would be by Fox

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.165
or by Republican members of Congress?

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:47.267
Oh, they would

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.002
threaten to burn it completely down.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.369
I mean,

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.703
I think that we all know

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.505
what that response would be.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.673
And it's unique

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.141
that you ask that question.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.910
And I think it's a very good question

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.312
because we now know that

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.079
many of the hosts

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.981
over at Fox News, the Tucker Carlson,

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.183
the Sean Hannity,

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.551
they get the leeway to say

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:04.884
whatever

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.553
they want to say, whether or not

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.788
it has veracity or not.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.689
It's it's

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:10.890
something that I would argue

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.158
that Jake Tapper doesn't have

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.059
is something I would argue

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.727
that Joy Reid doesn't have,

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.129
that you just don't have that leeway.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.697
And Jake, in your case specifically,

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.131
you don't have

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.199
that want

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.000
to go out there and mislead viewers

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.036
the way that we now know

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.205
Fox News host and contributors did.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.940
And I think that's a fundamental problem.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:27.907
And I think that.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.642
And Jonah knows Rupert Murdoch

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.477
better than I don't know him at all.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.145
He probably doesn't

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.413
know me from a can of paint.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.380
But I would also go a step

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.815
further and argue that

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:37.183
Rupert

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.017
Murdoch has

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:38.885
not only tarnished

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.486
and damaged his legacy,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.890
but he's also done a great deal of damage

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.992
to democracy throughout the world.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.994
Or democracies throughout the world,

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.562
because these lies

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.564
fundamentally erode what we believe

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.766
our democracy to be.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.568
And the fact that he had his soldiers

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.103
and lieutenants carrying it out

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:57.971
should be a problem.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.672
But no, I don't believe any host to CNN

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.574
or any host at MSNBC

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.142
particularly can get away

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.010
with the same things

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.311
that Tucker and Sean get away

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.713
with, particularly with these lies.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.981
So, Jonah, there's now attention

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.881
turning toward the

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.016
Fox board of directors.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.117
One of its members,

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.218
former Republican House Speaker

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.621
Paul Ryan, is trying to defend

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.089
his role

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.824
behind the scenes in a new interview with

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:18.992
Charlie Sykes. Take a listen.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.060
If you

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.061
are on the board of

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.162
directors of a company

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.131
that is pumping toxic sludge

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.367
racism, disinformation

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.203
and attacks on democracy,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.505
if you don't stand up now,

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.906
then when I do,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.874
I have a responsibility off

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.109
my opinion and perspective.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:36.609
And I do that.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.378
But I don't go on and TV and do it right.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.846
And so I have a response to you.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.114
I do. I do.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.283
So I offer my perspective in my opinion.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:43.883
Often

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:44.884
I think Fox is a big

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.019
part of the constellation.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:46.919
The conservative movement

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.088
isn't really a solution or the problem.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:49.589
Oh, no.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.357
I think it's going to have to be

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.158
a part of the solution

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.326
if we're going to solve the problem.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.128
The conservative movement

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.231
What do you think, Jonah, is Fox?

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.099
Obviously, they disagree.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.167
Is he part of the problem

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.702
or part is Fox part of the problem

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.403
or part of the solution

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.737
when it comes to conservatives?

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:07.040
Yeah.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:07.440
I mean,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.208
I had this very conversation

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.209
with Paul Ryan myself.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.644
Full disclosure, he's a friend of mine.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.013
And I got to say,

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.148
I disagree with Paul.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.382
And to a certain extent,

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.550
insofar as I think

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.785
turning the ship around.

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.620
Look, I was at Fox News for 12 years.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.822
I will still defend to this day.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.357
A lot of the people on in the news

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.358
division who,

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:27.360
you know, look we know from these filings

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.795
we're trying to push back on this,

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:29.462
which is why Tucker

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.030
and some people wanted to get them fired

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.498
because they were fact-checking

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.166
the nonsense

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.134
that was coming from the opinion side

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:35.702
and that was

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.737
what was pissing off the executives.

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:38.404
So I mean I think it's a

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.572
more nuanced problem

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.239
than a lot of people

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.475
want it to be at the same time.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.844
I think Paul is very sincere and honest

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.714
when he says that he's counseled this

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.349
from the get go, that

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.650
that that this stuff

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.318
is poisonous to the Fox brand.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.420
It's poisonous to conservatism.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.988
I just think what the current leadership

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.457
at Fox, particularly Susan Scott,

00:05:57.457 --> 00:06:00.927
the CEO who basically just gave the booze

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.829
and car keys to the fastest drivers,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.832
is not

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.835
is not currently situated

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.436
to make that transition.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.204
But yeah,

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.105
if if

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.306
if the conservative movement

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.775
and the Republican Party

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:17.443
can't turn Fox around

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.011
and make it a constructive part

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:19.979
of American discourse

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.614
and democracy in journalism,

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.349
then it's bad for the country,

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.751
but it's also bad for conservatism.

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:25.118
And I think

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.185
Paul Paul Ryan,

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.520
at the end of the day, cares a lot.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.621
You know, he's a party guy.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.256
He is a movement conservative.

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:31.591
He cares about those causes

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.092
and those institutions.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:34.761
I just think that

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:37.697
the task cut out for him to institute

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:40.400
reforms from within is is Herculean.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.935
McCarthy Last thoughts

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.738
No, I'm just admiring

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.006
Jonah's very vivid

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.275
analogies that he's using the day.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.077
But I actually agree

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:53.613
I wholeheartedly agree with with what

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:54.981
Paul Ryan said,

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.449
especially when it comes to the fact

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:56.983
that if

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.351
the conservative movement

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.552
is going to change,

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.286
if they're going to root out

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.020
these cancers,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.422
then Fox is going to be

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.222
a big part of that.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.257
The question I have, though,

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.224
is can they do that

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.793
under the leadership of Rupert Murdoch?

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:07.560
Can they do that

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.961
under the current leadership?

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.329
I think that's the largest question

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.432
that they're reading, those depositions.

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:13.366
And Jonah, thanks so much.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.300
Appreciate both of you.

